#1 Attributes and IDs

An `[attribute-list]` provides metadata to a node; it is not the same as a `[content]` span. Determine the construct from its leading marker and context before interpreting the brackets.

#2 Named attributes

Directive metadata uses `key=value`. Quote strings containing spaces. Whitespace between the directive name and attributes is optional.

```sm
&note[title="More details"]
This directive has a title.
&end

&note [title="Equivalent spacing"]
The space after the name is allowed.
&end
```

#2 Boolean flags

A flag such as `[typing]` is shorthand for a boolean true. The directive schema still determines whether a flag is supported.

```sm
&test[typing]
An example test.
&end
```

#2 Explicit IDs

Headings can use a trailing `(#id)`. Identifiers use Unicode NFC normalization and must be unique within a document.

```sm
#2 Document structure (#structure)

See &ref[structure] for details.
```

#2 Diagnostics

Invalid attributes and duplicate IDs should generate source-located diagnostics. A converter must preserve or report changes to their meaning.
